---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy – In-Between Labs"
  description="How Sigil Synth processes images and music locally and handles advertising data and privacy choices."
  canonical="https://inbetweenlabs.com/privacy-policy"
>
  <main class="container py-12 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="card p-8 md:p-12">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-white/60 text-sm">Last updated: October 14, 2026</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          This policy covers Sigil Synth, an Android image-to-music app published by In-Between Labs.
          Pi Drive Transfer is a separate personal
          utility with its own <a href="/pi-drive-transfer/privacy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">privacy notice</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Images, music and app accounts</h2>
        <p>
          Sigil Synth analyzes your selected images and generates music locally on your device. It stores temporary
          preview audio in its cache and saves WAV exports to your device's music storage. The app's music tools do not
          upload your selected images or generated audio to In-Between Labs servers. Your document provider,
          device backup service and device settings may have their own data practices.
        </p>
        <p>
          You do not need an app account to use Sigil Synth. The app does not ask for your name, email address or
          phone number to create music. If you contact us by email, we receive the address and information you send
          and use them to respond to your request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Advertising and data sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Sigil Synth displays ads through Google AdMob and the Google Mobile Ads SDK. Advertising involves data
          collection and sharing with Google and applicable advertising partners, even though your creative media
          is processed locally. These advertising identifiers and activity data are not necessarily anonymous.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on your device, region, privacy choices and advertising configuration, advertising services
          may collect and share your IP address, device or other identifiers, app and ad interactions, and diagnostic
          and performance information. An IP address may be used to estimate approximate location. Identifiers may
          include the Android advertising ID when available and permitted, app set ID and publisher first-party ID.
          These data support advertising, measurement and analytics, and security and fraud prevention, as applicable.
          App set ID supports reporting and fraud prevention rather than advertising personalization.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sigil Synth does not request Android precise-location permission. The consent message describes the
          partners' declared purposes and any special features for which they request permission; this does not mean
          that the app supplies every category a partner declares.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where a European consent message is shown, use <strong>Manage options</strong> and its partner list to see
          the advertising partners, their privacy policies, purposes and available choices. AdMob's partner list can
          change over time. Google documents its data handling in its
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Mobile Ads SDK data disclosure</a>,
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Privacy Policy</a>
          and
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">information about partner apps</a>.
          Google states that data collected by its Mobile Ads SDK is encrypted in transit using TLS.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Your advertising privacy choices</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google's User Messaging Platform for applicable privacy messages. Our European message is targeted
          to users in the EEA, United Kingdom and Switzerland and offers <strong>Consent</strong>,
          <strong>Do not consent</strong> and <strong>Manage options</strong>. You can choose the purposes and partners
          for which you grant consent and object to processing shown as legitimate interest. Some essential purposes,
          such as security and communicating privacy choices, cannot be switched off in the message.
        </p>
        <p>
          In app versions that include consent controls, use <strong>Ad privacy choices</strong> when available to
          review, change or withdraw your choices. The <strong>Privacy policy</strong> entry links to this page.
          Those versions check Google's
          ad-eligibility result before requesting ads; declining consent does not necessarily prevent all limited
          or non-personalized ads or all related data processing. The music tools remain usable when advertising
          is unavailable.
        </p>
        <p>
          Android's advertising settings may let you reset or delete your advertising ID. This does not necessarily
          stop other SDK identifiers or data handling.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Diagnostics and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Sigil Synth does not integrate a separate custom analytics service. Google Mobile Ads and related services
          can nevertheless process app and ad interactions, SDK diagnostics and performance information. Android
          and Google Play may also process diagnostic information under their own settings and policies.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Storage, retention and requests</h2>
        <p>
          Temporary preview files remain in app storage until removed by the app or Android storage controls.
          Exported music remains in device music storage until removed and may remain after uninstalling.
          You can manage local data using Android's app-storage and file tools. Backup or document providers may
          retain their own copies under their policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google and other advertising partners determine retention for the advertising data they process under
          their policies. Consent choices are stored on your device by Google's consent platform and can be
          replaced when you change them. Withdrawing consent does not itself delete data already held by a provider.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact us with privacy questions or data requests at
          <a href="mailto:inbetweenlabs@gmail.com" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">inbetweenlabs@gmail.com</a>.
          Tell us which app and request you mean. We can address our own practices and information we hold;
          requests concerning provider-held advertising data may also need to be directed to that provider through
          the privacy policies linked above or in the consent message.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Sigil Synth is not directed toward children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal
          information to us, please contact us using the address above.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy when the app or its data practices change. The date above identifies the latest
          policy update.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10">
        <a href="/" class="btn-ghost">← Back to In-Between Labs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

